# CI coverage exemptions — services/apps intentionally without a CI workflow.
#
# Format: one relative path per line (matching scripts/check-ci-coverage.sh
# output), blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# Prefer adding tests over exempting. Exempt only when the code is pure
# hardware glue or generated assets that can't be exercised off-device.
#
# There are currently NO exemptions. `services/oled-display` was the only
# entry and was removed in WARP-2685: its suite has run in CI since
# WARP-1640/1641 (.github/workflows/oled-display-panel-tests.yml, the whole
# tests/ directory bar one disk-layout-coupled file). The entry survived only
# because the checker resolved workflows by filename and could not see the
# `-panel-` infix; it now matches on the workflow's actual `paths:` filter.
#
# Before adding an entry here, check that the service really has no workflow —
# not merely no workflow named `<name>-tests.yml`.
